        "question_title": "Let \\(F(x)=\\int_0^x(t^2-4t+3)\\,dt\\). Which statement is correct?",
        "question_instruction": "Choose one correct option.",
        "explanation": "By the Fundamental Theorem of Calculus, \\(F'(x)=x^2-4x+3=(x-1)(x-3)\\). The sign pattern is positive, negative, positive across \\(1\\) and \\(3\\), so \\(x=1\\) is a local maximum and \\(x=3\\) is a local minimum.",
